  "notes": [
    "Mixed formats: the A division played single elimination, the B division played DOUBLE elimination with separate winners and losers brackets.",
    "The B division league phase was two parallel round robins, 'B (X)' and 'B (Z)', of 10 players each; the top 6 of each made the playoff with the top 2 getting a first-round bye.",
    "On the B brackets each name carries a number in parentheses \u2014 that is the player's rank within their own sub-group, which is why '(1)' appears twice (Steve is B(X) rank 1, Ryan is B(Z) rank 1). Verified against the standings: every one of the 12 B entrants matches.",
    "The B winners bracket ends 'Ryan over Terry'. Terry won the winners side; Ryan came back through the losers side and won the grand final. That is the double-elimination reset, so Ryan is champion and Terry runner-up.",
    "Steve lost the losers final to Ryan, which places him third.",
    "A division seeds match the Division A standings ranks exactly.",
    "Standings are a PNG screenshot with no text layer and were read visually.",
    "No scores are recorded on any of the three brackets, only winners.",
    "Michael appears here as 'KnotYourCapitan' \u2014 see the note in data/players.json about the tournament 10 spelling.",
    "TournamentResults.pdf records a B division consolation bracket (Jayson champion, Brian runner-up) that has no bracket sheet in the source files."
  ],
